	(text_box "Route analog RX (RX_P, RX_N) and TX (TX_P, TX_N) pairs as differential signals with a 100 Ohm impedance profile, in a coplanar differential microstrip or stripline configuration.\n\nThe calculations for trace width have been made according to the manufacturing specs listed in the main architecture sheet of this PCB and assuming a coplanar differential routing approach (0.1mm clearance to GND, 0.2mm distance between differential signal taces).\n\nThe results of the JLCPCB online impedance calculator are the following:\n\nLayer 1 trace width = 0.1090 mm\nLayer 4 trace width = 0.1476 mm\nLayer 5 trace width = 0.1090 mm\n\nThe impedance profiles will only be accurate if the following aspects are specified when ordering:\n\nLayers = 6\nInner copper weight = 0.5oz\nOuter copper weight = 1oz\nPCB thickness = 1.6mm\nManufacturer = JLCPCB\nStack-up Code = JLC0616H-3313A"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 383.54 32.8422 0)
		(size -38.1 88.9)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "58b503b1-f8b4-48b3-9df4-d7f6c269ff5f")
	)
	(text_box "Keep all RMII traces below 150mm.\n\nAvoid using vias on RMII signals, if necessary, use the same number of vias for all signals.\n\nLength match the following signals to <5 mm:\n\nTXD0, TXD1, TXEN, length matched to each other (RMII_TX net class).\n\nRXD0, RXD1, CRS, length matched to each other (RMII_RX net class).\n\nPHY_CLK_50M, MCU_CLK_50M, length matched to each other (RMII_SYNC net class)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 299.72 91.2622 0)
		(size -50.8 40.64)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
